---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

// Depths are read off the build scripts, not estimated. 02_wall.py cuts the
// face from Z 0.30 down to -6.30; 04_tiles.py starts tile 0 at Z 0.15 and takes
// one metre per tile. Horizon boundaries are the midpoints of the fades in
// 03_material.py BOUNDS.
const horizons = [
  { key: 'O', name: 'Litter', depth: '0 to 6 cm', note: 'Leaf duff, not yet soil. The only horizon you ever see.' },
  { key: 'A', name: 'Topsoil', depth: '6 to 56 cm', note: 'Dark umber. Organic matter mixed down into mineral grain.' },
  { key: 'B', name: 'Subsoil', depth: '56 cm to 2.3 m', note: 'Red clay. Everything washed out of A has accumulated here.' },
  { key: 'C', name: 'Regolith', depth: '2.3 to 4.7 m', note: 'Pale ochre. Parent rock, broken but not yet moved.' },
  { key: 'R', name: 'Bedrock', depth: 'below 4.7 m', note: 'Cool grey. Roots stop at 2.7 m, well short of it.' },
];
---

<Base
  title="The Underground · Lab · Brett Boggs"
  description="A six metre soil profile you descend by scrolling, rendered in Blender. Roots grow as you go."
  scene="lab"
>
  <article>
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Lab · Aug 2026</p>
      <h1>The Underground</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The Ridge looks at the grass. This is the same ground from the side, cut open six metres
        down to rock. Scroll and the roots grow with you.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        A real soil profile has five horizons, and only the top one is ever visible. The rest is
        ordinary, universal and completely hidden, which seemed worth six metres of scroll.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <div class="wall-shell">
    <div class="wall" id="ug-wall"></div>
    <aside class="rod" id="ug-rod" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="rod-depth" id="ug-depth">0.0 m</span>
      <span class="rod-horizon" id="ug-horizon">Litter</span>
    </aside>
  </div>

  <article>
    <section class="bed">
      <p class="bed-note">Bedrock. Nothing grows through that.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>The profile</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing here is stylised. The colour arc is real reflectance: dry topsoil sits near 0.10 to
        0.15 albedo, and mineral horizons get paler with depth because they carry less organic
        matter. An early pass used 0.06 for topsoil and the whole face went to mud.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="horizons">
      {
        horizons.map((h) => (
          <li>
            <span class="h-key">{h.key}</span>
            <span class="h-body">
              <span class="h-name">{h.name}</span>
              <span class="h-depth">{h.depth}</span>
              <span class="h-note">{h.note}</span>
            </span>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Growth without a video</h2>
      <p>
        Roots are not a frame sequence. Each root layer ships as a colour plate plus a data plate
        whose red channel holds the time that pixel was born, baked out of the growth simulation.
        The shader draws everything born before the current scroll depth and feathers the edge, so
        growth is continuous at any scroll speed, has no loop to seam, and costs two images instead
        of a film.
      </p>
      <p>
        The data plate has to be read raw. It is written as non colour data, so the byte is the
        value. Letting the browser apply an sRGB decode bent the timeline badly enough that half the
        growth landed in the first fifth of the scroll.
      </p>

      <h2>The lag is the trick</h2>
      <p>
        Driving growth straight off scroll position pins the growing front to one line of the screen,
        because birth time is depth and the wall scrolls exactly one metre per tile. Nothing ever
        changes where you are looking. Chasing the target instead of matching it means every scroll
        leaves the tips behind and you watch them catch up.
      </p>

      <h2>What moves, and what does not</h2>
      <p>
        There are no worms. Roots, mycelium, water and rock only, which leaves very little honest
        movement in a static face. Roots growing works because roots grow. Loose crumbs work because
        you are the disturbance: they spawn against scroll distance, live in document coordinates so
        they fall down the wall they came out of, and land under real gravity.
      </p>
      <p>
        Moisture does not move, deliberately. Four attempts at animating the damp patches, drifting
        sheen, per patch pulse, specular glint, all read as a film laid over the wall rather than as
        wet ground, and none of them were perceptible to the person looking. A ten second moisture
        pulse was invented. The patches are baked into the plates and stay put.
      </p>

      <h2>Light</h2>
      <p>
        One number does the lighting. The cut is a slot 1.6 m wide with camera invisible blockers, so
        the open sky above is the only source. Sky visibility falls with the width of that opening,
        which is what makes the descent go dark on its own, and 1.6 m puts the shadow line about a
        third of the way down.
      </p>

      <h2>Still open</h2>
      <p>
        Roots stop at 2.7 m, so the bottom two tiles carry nothing but rock and are the least
        interesting scroll on the page. Mycelium is one tile where it should probably be three. The
        wall is a single column, so a wide monitor gets a tall thin strip of soil with a lot of paper
        either side.
      </p>
    </div>

    <a class="back-link" href="/lab/">Back to Lab</a>
  </article>
</Base>

<script>
  const A = '/lab/underground/';
  const wall = document.getElementById('ug-wall');
  const depthOut = document.getElementById('ug-depth');
  const horizonOut = document.getElementById('ug-horizon');
  const rod = document.getElementById('ug-rod');

  const reduced = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

  // Same geometry the tiles were rendered on: 04_tiles.py TILE_TOP_Z and one
  // metre per tile. Boundaries are the fade midpoints from 03_material.py.
  const WALL_TOP_Z = 0.15;
  const BIRTH_TOP = 0.12;
  const BIRTH_END = -2.15;
  const FRONT_AT = 0.52;
  const EASE = 0.022;
  const N_TILES = 6;
  const BANDS = [
    { z: 0.15, name: 'Litter' },
    { z: -0.06, name: 'Topsoil' },
    { z: -0.56, name: 'Subsoil' },
    { z: -2.33, name: 'Regolith' },
    { z: -4.73, name: 'Bedrock' },
  ];

  function readout() {
    if (!wall || !rod || !depthOut || !horizonOut) return;
    const r = wall.getBoundingClientRect();
    const showing = r.bottom > 0 && r.top < innerHeight;
    rod.classList.toggle('is-on', showing);
    if (!showing) return;
    const tileH = r.height / N_TILES;
    if (!tileH) return;
    const z = WALL_TOP_Z - ((FRONT_AT * innerHeight) - r.top) / tileH;
    const depth = Math.max(0, -z);
    depthOut.textContent = depth.toFixed(1) + ' m';
    let name = BANDS[0].name;
    for (const b of BANDS) if (z <= b.z) name = b.name;
    horizonOut.textContent = name;
  }

  if (wall) start();

  async function start() {
    const manifest = await (await fetch(A + 'manifest.json')).json();

    const tiles = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < manifest.tiles; i++) {
      const d = document.createElement('div');
      d.className = 'tile';
      const img = new Image();
      img.src = A + 'tile_' + i + '.webp';
      img.alt =
        i === 0
          ? 'The top of an excavated soil face: leaf litter, dark topsoil and the first roots.'
          : '';
      img.width = manifest.tile.w;
      img.height = manifest.tile.h;
      img.decoding = 'async';
      if (i > 1) img.loading = 'lazy';
      d.appendChild(img);
      wall.appendChild(d);
      tiles.push(d);
    }

    const VERT = [
      '#version 300 es',
      'in vec2 p; out vec2 uv;',
      'void main(){ uv = vec2((p.x+1.0)*0.5, 1.0-(p.y+1.0)*0.5);',
      '             gl_Position = vec4(p,0.0,1.0); }',
    ].join('\n');

    // Reads the timing map RAW. The data plates are written as Non-Color data,
    // so the byte IS the value; an sRGB decode here bends the timeline badly.
    const FRAG = [
      '#version 300 es',
      'precision highp float;',
      'in vec2 uv; out vec4 outColor;',
      'uniform sampler2D uColor;',
      'uniform sampler2D uData;',
      'uniform float uProgress, uFeather, uFront;',
      'void main(){',
      '  vec4 c = texture(uColor, uv);',
      '  if (c.a < 0.004) { outColor = vec4(0.0); return; }',
      '  float born = texture(uData, uv).r;',
      '  float vis = clamp((uProgress - born)/uFeather, 0.0, 1.0);',
      '  float g = (uProgress - born)/(uFeather*0.8);',
      '  float front = exp(-g*g) * uFront;',
      '  float a = c.a * vis;',
      '  outColor = vec4((c.rgb + front) * a, a);',
      '}',
    ].join('\n');

    function makeLayer(host, colorURL, dataURL, opts) {
      opts = opts || {};
      const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
      host.appendChild(canvas);
      const gl = canvas.getContext('webgl2', { alpha: true, premultipliedAlpha: true });
      if (!gl) return null;

      const sh = (type, src) => {
        const o = gl.createShader(type);
        gl.shaderSource(o, src);
        gl.compileShader(o);
        if (!gl.getShaderParameter(o, gl.COMPILE_STATUS)) {
          throw new Error(gl.getShaderInfoLog(o) || 'shader');
        }
        return o;
      };
      const prog = gl.createProgram();
      gl.attachShader(prog, sh(gl.VERTEX_SHADER, VERT));
      gl.attachShader(prog, sh(gl.FRAGMENT_SHADER, FRAG));
      gl.linkProgram(prog);
      if (!gl.getProgramParameter(prog, gl.LINK_STATUS)) {
        throw new Error(gl.getProgramInfoLog(prog) || 'link');
      }
      gl.useProgram(prog);

      gl.bindVertexArray(gl.createVertexArray());
      gl.bindBuffer(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, gl.createBuffer());
      gl.bufferData(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, new Float32Array([-1, -1, 3, -1, -1, 3]), gl.STATIC_DRAW);
      const loc = gl.getAttribLocation(prog, 'p');
      gl.enableVertexAttribArray(loc);
      gl.vertexAttribPointer(loc, 2, gl.FLOAT, false, 0, 0);

      const uProgress = gl.getUniformLocation(prog, 'uProgress');
      gl.uniform1i(gl.getUniformLocation(prog, 'uColor'), 0);
      gl.uniform1i(gl.getUniformLocation(prog, 'uData'), 1);
      gl.uniform1f(gl.getUniformLocation(prog, 'uFeather'), opts.feather || 0.05);
      gl.uniform1f(gl.getUniformLocation(prog, 'uFront'), opts.front || 0.2);
      gl.enable(gl.BLEND);
      gl.blendFunc(gl.ONE, gl.ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA);
      gl.clearColor(0, 0, 0, 0);

      const layer = { last: 0, ready: false, draw: () => {} };

      (async () => {
        const pairs = [
          [colorURL, 0],
          [dataURL, 1],
        ];
        for (const pair of pairs) {
          const img = new Image();
          img.src = pair[0];
          await img.decode();
          gl.activeTexture(gl.TEXTURE0 + pair[1]);
          gl.bindTexture(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.createTexture());
          // never let the browser premultiply: the shader does it, and the data
          // texture must survive upload untouched
          gl.pixelStorei(gl.UNPACK_PREMULTIPLY_ALPHA_WEBGL, false);
          gl.texImage2D(gl.TEXTURE_2D, 0, gl.RGBA8, gl.RGBA, gl.UNSIGNED_BYTE, img);
          gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_MIN_FILTER, gl.LINEAR);
          gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_MAG_FILTER, gl.LINEAR);
          gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_WRAP_S, gl.CLAMP_TO_EDGE);
          gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_WRAP_T, gl.CLAMP_TO_EDGE);
        }
        layer.ready = true;
        layer.draw(layer.last);
      })();

      layer.draw = (p) => {
        layer.last = p;
        if (!layer.ready) return;
        const r = host.getBoundingClientRect();
        const dpr = Math.min(devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);
        const w = Math.max(1, Math.round(r.width * dpr));
        const h = Math.max(1, Math.round(r.height * dpr));
        if (canvas.width !== w || canvas.height !== h) {
          canvas.width = w;
          canvas.height = h;
        }
        gl.viewport(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);
        gl.clear(gl.COLOR_BUFFER_BIT);
        gl.uniform1f(uProgress, p);
        gl.drawArrays(gl.TRIANGLES, 0, 3);
      };
      return layer;
    }

    const OPTS = {
      root: { feather: 0.055, front: 0.14 },
      myc: { feather: 0.07, front: 0.26 },
    };
    const groups = {};
    for (const kind of Object.keys(manifest.features)) {
      groups[kind] = [];
      for (let i = 0; i < manifest.features[kind].tiles; i++) {
        const l = makeLayer(
          tiles[i],
          A + kind + '_' + i + '.webp',
          A + kind + 'time_' + i + '.webp',
          OPTS[kind]
        );
        if (l) groups[kind].push(l);
      }
    }

    // Reduced motion gets the finished wall: everything grown, no crumbs, no
    // chase. The page still reads, it just does not animate.
    if (reduced) {
      for (const kind of Object.keys(groups)) groups[kind].forEach((l) => l.draw(1));
      readout();
      addEventListener('scroll', readout, { passive: true });
      addEventListener('resize', readout);
      return;
    }

    // ---------------------------------------------------------------- crumbs --
    // The one piece of movement not on a clock: the reader scrolling IS the
    // disturbance. Particles live in DOCUMENT coordinates so a crumb falls down
    // the wall it came out of; a fixed canvas draws them at docY - scrollY.
    const crumbCanvas = document.createElement('canvas');
    crumbCanvas.className = 'crumbs';
    document.body.appendChild(crumbCanvas);
    const cx = crumbCanvas.getContext('2d');
    const crumbImg = new Image();
    crumbImg.src = A + 'crumbs.webp';
    let crumbReady = false;
    crumbImg
      .decode()
      .then(() => {
        crumbReady = true;
      })
      .catch(() => {});

    const CRUMB_CELL = 64;
    const CRUMB_N = 8;
    const GRAVITY = 5200;
    const MAX_CRUMBS = 260;
    const crumbs = [];
    let lastScroll = scrollY;
    let spawnBudget = 0;

    function spawnCrumbs() {
      const d = Math.abs(scrollY - lastScroll);
      lastScroll = scrollY;
      if (!crumbReady || d < 1) return;
      const r = wall.getBoundingClientRect();
      if (r.bottom < 0 || r.top > innerHeight) return;
      // more disturbance shakes more loose, capped so a fling does not dump a
      // hundred crumbs at once
      spawnBudget += Math.min(d, 90) * 0.17;
      const top = Math.max(r.top, 0);
      const bot = Math.min(r.bottom, innerHeight);
      while (spawnBudget >= 1 && crumbs.length < MAX_CRUMBS) {
        spawnBudget -= 1;
        const sy = top + Math.random() * Math.max(1, bot - top);
        crumbs.push({
          x: r.left + Math.random() * r.width,
          y: sy + scrollY,
          vx: (Math.random() - 0.5) * 40,
          vy: Math.random() * 30,
          rot: Math.random() * 6.28,
          spin: (Math.random() - 0.5) * 7,
          size: 5 + Math.random() * 11,
          cell: Math.floor(Math.random() * CRUMB_N),
          life: 0,
        });
      }
    }

    function drawCrumbs(dt) {
      if (!cx) return;
      const dpr = Math.min(devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);
      const w = Math.round(innerWidth * dpr);
      const h = Math.round(innerHeight * dpr);
      if (crumbCanvas.width !== w || crumbCanvas.height !== h) {
        crumbCanvas.width = w;
        crumbCanvas.height = h;
      }
      cx.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);
      cx.clearRect(0, 0, innerWidth, innerHeight);
      if (!crumbReady) return;
      for (let i = crumbs.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
        const c = crumbs[i];
        c.life += dt;
        c.vy += GRAVITY * dt;
        c.vx *= 1 - 1.6 * dt;
        c.x += c.vx * dt;
        c.y += c.vy * dt;
        c.rot += c.spin * dt;
        const sy = c.y - scrollY;
        if (sy > innerHeight + 40 || c.life > 6) {
          crumbs.splice(i, 1);
          continue;
        }
        cx.save();
        cx.translate(c.x, sy);
        cx.rotate(c.rot);
        cx.globalAlpha = Math.min(1, c.life * 8);
        cx.drawImage(
          crumbImg,
          c.cell * CRUMB_CELL,
          0,
          CRUMB_CELL,
          CRUMB_CELL,
          -c.size / 2,
          -c.size / 2,
          c.size,
          c.size
        );
        cx.restore();
      }
      cx.globalAlpha = 1;
    }

    // ---------------------------------------------------------------- scroll --
    function targets() {
      const r = wall.getBoundingClientRect();
      const tileH = r.height / N_TILES;
      if (!tileH) return { root: 0, myc: 0 };
      const z = WALL_TOP_Z - ((FRONT_AT * innerHeight) - r.top) / tileH;
      const root = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, (BIRTH_TOP - z) / (BIRTH_TOP - BIRTH_END)));
      const myc = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, (root - 0.05) / 0.42));
      return { root: root, myc: myc };
    }

    const cur = { root: 0, myc: 0 };
    const drawn = { root: -1, myc: -1 };
    let onScreen = true;
    let lastNow = 0;

    function frame(now) {
      requestAnimationFrame(frame);
      const dt = Math.min(0.05, lastNow ? (now - lastNow) / 1000 : 0.016);
      lastNow = now;
      if (!onScreen) return;
      spawnCrumbs();
      drawCrumbs(dt);
      // The lag is what makes growth perceptible: chasing the target leaves the
      // tips behind and you watch them catch up.
      const tgt = targets();
      for (const kind of Object.keys(groups)) {
        cur[kind] += (tgt[kind] - cur[kind]) * EASE;
        if (Math.abs(cur[kind] - drawn[kind]) > 0.0012) {
          groups[kind].forEach((l) => l.draw(cur[kind]));
          drawn[kind] = cur[kind];
        }
      }
      readout();
    }

    new IntersectionObserver(
      (es) => {
        onScreen = es.some((e) => e.isIntersecting);
      },
      { rootMargin: '200px' }
    ).observe(wall);

    // The rod also has to update when the loop is parked, otherwise scrolling
    // past the wall leaves it on screen showing the last depth it saw.
    addEventListener('scroll', readout, { passive: true });
    addEventListener('resize', readout);
    readout();
    requestAnimationFrame(frame);
  }
</script>

<style>
  /* 100vw includes the scrollbar, so a full bleed shell overflows sideways */
  .wall-shell {
    position: relative;
    width: 100vw;
    margin-left: calc(50% - 50vw);
    margin-top: 3rem;
    overflow-x: hidden;
  }
  .wall {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--ink);
    border-right: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .wall :global(.tile) {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
  }
  .wall :global(.tile img) {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    margin-bottom: -1px; /* kills the seam at fractional DPR */
  }
  .wall :global(.tile canvas) {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  :global(canvas.crumbs) {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 5;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .rod {
    position: fixed;
    right: clamp(0.8rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    top: 50%;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    z-index: 6;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.15rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.7rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--sienna);
    background: rgba(244, 237, 223, 0.82);
    backdrop-filter: blur(4px);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.4s var(--ease-warm);
  }
  .rod.is-on {
    opacity: 1;
  }
  .rod-depth {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .rod-horizon {
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .rod {
      top: auto;
      bottom: 1rem;
      right: 1rem;
      transform: none;
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: baseline;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }
  }

  .bed {
    margin: 0 0 3rem;
    padding-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  .bed-note {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .horizons {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 2.4rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.9rem;
  }
  .horizons li {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    border-top: 2px solid rgba(51, 41, 28, 0.16);
    padding-top: 0.7rem;
  }
  .h-key {
    flex: none;
    width: 1.4em;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--sienna);
  }
  .h-body {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.15rem;
  }
  .h-name {
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .h-depth,
  .h-note {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .rod {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
